==Battleground==
*3 [[Wild Doge]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 23.33~30 seconds<sup>700f~900f</sup>.
*1 [[Imperator Sael]] spawns after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.
*2 [[J.J. Jackrabbit]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Alpacky]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Wild Doge]]s spawn, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
**8 [[Wild Doge]]s spawn, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
**8 [[J.J. Jackrabbit]]s spawn, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
**3 [[Wild Doge]]s spawn, delay 4 seconds<sup>120f</sup>.
**4 [[Helmut Krabbe]]s spawn, delay 23.33~30 seconds<sup>700f~900f</sup>.
**3 [[Imperator Sael]]s spawn, delay 46.67~50 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,500f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The key to this stage is having a strong frontline mixed with heavy hitting rushers who can actually make it to the base in time and deal meaningful DPS.

If you have [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Castaway Cat]], [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]], and every relevant treasure from [[Into the Future]], this stage should be far easier as all enemies will be buffed to their intended percentage. Be careful with your Awakened Bahamut timing, try to catch Alpacky during a time period where she is completely unguarded. Otherwise, Bahamut will be juggled, leading to a potential loss.

